k-words">This IP policy governs ownership of creative works and inventions =
at The Principia (a teaching institution).</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Key Points:</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-2.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Default ownership</stro=
ng>: Creators retain rights to their intellectual property</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Four major exceptions</=
strong> where Principia claims ownership:
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-2.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Written contracts specifying ot=
herwise</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Commissioned "work for hire"</l=
i>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Administrative works created du=
ring employment</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Works using "substantial" Princ=
ipia resources (beyond normal office space, utilities, standard equipment)<=
/li>
</ol>
</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Revenue split</strong>:=
 50/50 between creator and institution for Principia-owned IP</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Educational courseware<=
/strong>: Exempt from institutional ownership unless it creates expenses ex=
ceeding $5,000</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Dispute resolution</str=
ong>: Mediation then arbitration (Principia pays most costs)</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Concerns for employees:<=
/strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-2.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The "substantial use" exception=
 is somewhat vague despite examples</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Disclosure requirements before =
commercialization</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Cannot use Principia's name in =
outside consulting without permission</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Assessment</strong>: Thi=
s policy is <strong>notably more creator-friendly than typical academic IP =
policies</strong>. Most universities claim broader ownership over faculty i=
nventions and research, especially in STEM fields. The 50/50 revenue split =
and creator-retention default are generous compared to standard academic ag=
reements.</p></div></div></div><div class=3D"absolute bottom-0 right-2 poin=
